# LegislAI Agentic Architecture

Read `AGENTS.md` and `.cursor/resources/agent-roster.md` before multi-file work.

## Pipeline order

ETL → Database → Analysis → Gemini Ops (quota/model/ops-log) → API/Routes → Frontend → QA

Upstream changes must produce a handoff (skill `legislai-pipeline-handoff`) so downstream layers accept the new shape and the UI can show it.

## Role selection

| Work touches | Load skill / act as |
|--------------|---------------------|
| Cross-layer feature | `legislai-orchestrate` |
| Congress/RSS/processors/backfill | `legislai-etl` |
| `db_models.py` / migrations | `legislai-database` |
| Gemini analyzer / categories / hidden provisions | `legislai-analysis` |
| `templates/` / `static/` | `legislai-frontend` |
| Tests / display_ready verification | `legislai-qa` |

Prefer Task subagents with clear ownership boundaries from the roster. Pass handoff packets between them.

